st - manage stacked diffs on top of git

usage: st <command> [args]

commands:
  abort              Abort an in-progress restack/rebase, restoring the prior state
  absorb             Absorb staged hunks into the stack commits that own their lines
  bottom (b)         Jump to the bottom branch of the current stack (just above trunk)
  checkout (co)      Check out a tracked branch (lists branches if no name)
  completion         Print a shell completion script (bash|zsh|fish)
  continue           Resume a restack that was interrupted by a merge conflict
  create (c)         Create a new branch stacked on the current branch
  delete (rm)        Delete a branch and re-parent its children
  down (d)           Move down the stack toward trunk
  fold               Fold the current branch into its parent (parent absorbs its commits)
  guide              Print the recommended stacked-diff workflow
  init               Initialize stacked stack tracking in this repo
  log (ls)           Show the stack as a tree
  modify (amend, m)  Amend (or add) a commit on the current branch and restack everything above
  onto (move)        Move the current branch (and its upstack) onto a new parent
  rename (mv)        Rename a branch and update the stack metadata
  repair             Reconcile the stack metadata with the repository (fix drift)
  restack (r)        Rebase the current branch and everything above it onto their parents
  shell              Print the shell integration that teleports into a branch's worktree
  squash             Squash all of the current branch's commits into one
  status (stat)      Show current branch, its parent/children, and restack state
  submit (ss)        Push every branch in the current stack to the remote (no PRs — login-free)
  sync (s)           Fetch trunk, fast-forward it, restack everything, and prune merged branches
  top (t)            Jump to the top of the current stack
  track              Start tracking the current git branch in the stack
  undo               Undo the last stack-mutating command
  untrack            Stop tracking a branch (re-parents its children)
  up (u)             Move up the stack to a child branch
  validate (doctor)  Check the stack state for drift or inconsistencies
  worktree (wt)      Materialize, list, or remove a branch's own worktree
  help               show this help
  version            print the version

New here? Run "st guide" for the recommended workflow, or "st status" to see where you are.
